      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems to be a pretty common standard for the pd_task in particular with 13 other boards already adopting magic numbers, either 1000 or 1280 bytes with the only constraint being this must be divisible by 4 for the word size. I didn\u0027t see any commit hashes from git blame that indicated why that convention is chosen. There are PD_TASK_STACK_SIZE defined for some boards, but they\u0027re unused and nowhere near the size of the typical pd_task at 800 or 2048 bytes on the 2 chip configurations it\u0027s been defined in.\n\nThe most likely explanation I see is different boards enable different feature sets for the pd_task and this can have a significant impact on the required stack size. If you\u0027re trying to optimize for available memory, setting the PD_TASK_STACK_SIZE at the upper bounds will be unsuitable for boards with limited capabilities or enabled features.\n\nWe could define stack sizes on a per board basis with defines in the board.h, but right now that convention hasn\u0027t been used on any boards.",
      "parentUuid": "d899c6f4_1b9da689",
